<http://data.silknow.org/object/c3c0069d-1bc9-3d9a-9248-ff4a1e504251/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man’s doublet of black silk taffeta, with a supplementary weft of silver wire, interlined with linen and lined with bright yellow silk taffeta.  It has a 2¼-inch (5.4 cm) collar, 1¼-inch (3 cm) deep shoulder wings, curving 2-piece sleeves, with a high waist and 8 large, deep laps below the waist.  The belly pieces are made of bents (stems of rushes) stitched between layers of linen and covered with the yellow silk.  There are 7 worked buttonholes on each sleeve, 27 on the left front and 3 on the left collar.  The buttons have a domed wooden core covered with black silk floss and silver filè thread; 21 remain.  A lacing loop of yellow taffeta is sewn to each belly piece.  Around the waist of the doublet are 22 bows of 1¼-inch (3.1 cm) of gauze ribbon woven with silver filè and strip, each end bearing a silver repoussé aiguillette."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/c3c0069d-1bc9-3d9a-9248-ff4a1e504251> .

